# /redwood/etc/oslogfwd.filter -- what oslogfwd forwards to /dev/console.
#
# One process name per line.  A leading '#' is a comment; blank lines are skipped;
# a trailing '*' makes the name a prefix; "all" (or "*") means no process filter.
# The name is matched against the event's process name and against the basename of
# its path, case-insensitively, so "CommCenter" matches both "CommCenter" and
# "/System/Library/Frameworks/CoreTelephony.framework/Support/CommCenter".
#
# The boot-arg oslog_proc=a,b and the environment variables OSLOGFWD_FILTER (a list)
# and OSLOGFWD_FILTER_FILE (another path) override this file.  The level filter is
# Default+Error+Fault; oslog_levels=default,info,debug,error,fault or OSLOGFWD_LEVELS
# changes it.
CommCenter
nfcd
fileproviderd
mediaserverd
bluetoothd
locationd
SpringBoard
